# Review ownership. The last matching pattern wins.
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# A single owner while this is solo-maintained. An unresolvable owner — a team that does
# not exist — silently requests review from nobody, which is worse than naming one person,
# so switch these to @kdpa-llc/<team> only once that team actually exists.

* @moscaverd

# The contracts are the project. A change here changes what everything else must satisfy,
# so it should never land on a single reviewer's nod.
/docs/specs/                @moscaverd
/docs/adr/                  @moscaverd
/PROJECT_CONSTITUTION.md    @moscaverd

# The control plane is where the "no orchestration graph" invariant lives or dies.
/src/control-plane/         @moscaverd

# Anything touching the trust boundary: sandbox confinement, permissions, budgets.
/src/data-plane/sandbox/    @moscaverd
/src/control-plane/permissions.ts @moscaverd
/SECURITY.md                @moscaverd

/.github/                   @moscaverd
